<title>RUSSIA: Details of Russia's Q3 crude oil export schedule.</title>
<headline>Details of Russia's Q3 crude oil export schedule.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia plans to export 25.27 million tonnes (2.02 million barrels per day) of oil outside the Commonwealth of Independent States in the third quarter of 1997, according to the official loading schedule for that period.</p>
<p>The Fuel and Energy Ministry's schedule, a copy of which was obtained by Reuters, outlines 4.31 million tonnes of non-CIS exports to fund state-sponsored programmes and 20.96 million tonnes for producers.</p>
<p>It also outlines a further 870,000 tonnes of Kazakh transit oil to be transported to non-CIS destinations during the third quarter of 1997, and another 730,000 tonnes of Kazakh oil going to two Ukrainian refineries.</p>
<p>Export plans for the third quarter are slightly lower than overall non-CIS oil export rates throughout 1996, when Russia exported 105 million tonnes, or 2.1 million bpd.</p>
